@Priority W-3 is done and the lock is released. W-4 is ready, so please check its envelope (60 money, 3 model calls, 15 minutes, 2 retries). W-5 and W-6 stay on HOLD until their predecessor finishes. Rule: Dependency order with a single writer: run a workflow only when everything it depends on is done, and release the lock before the next run starts..
HOLD W-5: W-4 (prd-requirements) must finish first
HOLD W-6: W-5 (prd-success) must finish first

@Priority Run order is W-7, W-8, W-9, one at a time under my write lock. Please check the envelope of W-7 first (8 money, 2 model calls, 8 minutes, 1 retry). W-8 and W-9 wait their turn. Rule: Dependency order with a single writer: run a workflow only when everything it depends on is done, release the lock before the next run starts, and run revisions in section order (Problem, Requirements, Success metrics) as Identity directed..
HOLD W-8: W-7 (prd-problem-r2) must finish and release the write lock first
HOLD W-9: W-8 (prd-requirements-r2) must finish first, because it depends on the revised Requirements section and the lock
